# Brochure design

Admin can generate a landscape product brochure PDF from Sales list and the product page.

Rules:
- Universal black / white / ZK red (`#F90202`) template in `public/images/brochures/template-bg.png`
- Do not put the ZK logo lockup, the red ZK mark, or "Official F1 Paddock Club Distributor" on the pages
- Cover headline is the package name, with the event underneath and the circuit/location as small supporting text
- Page 2 is titled The Experience and shows the description as whole sentences. Stop at the last sentence that fits. Do not end a sentence with an ellipsis
- Page 3 is titled What's Included and shows the inclusion list as bullets. A long bullet may be shortened to two lines, but only on a finished phrase, with no ellipsis
- Each of those pages uses a few photos in the right-hand column, each with a thin ZK red border and even gaps. The two pages do not repeat the same photos. If there are not enough photos, use a one-photo or two-photo stack, or drop the photo column. Do not add further copy pages. The track-map page still follows when a map exists
- The track-map page is only created when the product has a track map image; title it The Details, show the full map uncropped, and list Location as a heading with the place name, in the same style as Event, Circuit, and Dates
- Black footer bar with a red line along the top and the page number on the right; no zk-sports.com address
- Photography-led, short readable copy — do not invent itineraries, partner logos, or prices
- Refuse to generate without at least 3 unique photos; prompt staff to add them
- Refuse to generate without a short description and at least 4 inclusions, unless the product is a standard F1 Paddock Club or Champions Club programme whose official copy we already store
- Keep generation CMS-staff only; portal clients may download an attached file, not create one
- Guest guide is a separate PDF next to the sales brochure on the admin product page. Do not show it on the agent portal. Cover page stays the sales cover; later pages use staff-edited guest guide copy. Empty pages are skipped. Do not invent itineraries, prices, or on-ground contact details
- Official Singapore Velocity Terrace guest guide only: cover uses the Velocity Terrace logo, then "Presented by" and the SY logo centred under it, then the event details centred on that same column; the supplied partner marks (SY, ZK, The Team) sit in the footer on every page; the closing page uses the National Gallery location map. Do not add those logos or that map to the shared guest-guide template or the sales brochure
- Guest guide pages are Welcome, Before race weekend, Digital ticket, Arriving, Experience, Getting there, Parking, On-ground support, Things to know, then the closing page. Discover QR/link lives on the closing page. On-ground contact lives on On-ground support. Red section headings use the bold condensed face
- Work lives in `lib/brochures/`, `lib/brochures/guest-guide/`, `components/admin/package-brochure-actions.tsx`, `components/admin/package-guest-guide-panel.tsx`, and `app/(admin)/admin/catalog/brochure-actions.ts`
